  "a5_policy": "a5 hard-fixes T_base_cube[s] = T_base_fk_raw[s] @ Delta_train for the 11 training placements, reusing the SAME Delta_train (aligned_fk_train/artifact) that factor_fk fits from those placements' eye-in-hand cube corners for this iteration -- see calibration_pipeline/schema.py's VISION_ALIGNED_FK_FIXED_CONTRACT and ALIGNED_FK_FIXED_ROWS. Held-out evaluation is identical to every other mode: reprojects the uncorrected/raw T_base_cube_FK[h] (never touched by any fit) through a5's fitted cameras.",
  "pose_comparison_policy": "For each iteration/mode, T_base_cube_vision_estimate[h] is a multi-camera bundle solve of ONLY the held-out cube pose against h's real corner detections, with every camera extrinsic (T_base_Ci, T_gripper_cam) frozen at that mode's fitted values from the training fit (solve_vision_only_cube_pose, reusing solve_corner_reprojection). Compared against the same independent T_base_cube_FK[h] via calibration_pipeline.reprojection.pose_delta: translation_mm is the Euclidean distance between the two poses' translations, rotation_deg is the angle-axis magnitude of the relative rotation inv(R_vision) @ R_fk.",
